# ~/.organism: machine-agnostic agent-harness code, symlink-deployed into ~/.claude.
#
# DENY BY DEFAULT. Only known code file types are committed; everything else
# (credentials, tokens, per-machine state, logs, caches, generated files) is
# ignored unless explicitly re-included below. The HARD RE-DENY block (§4)
# overrides the re-includes, so a secret can never be staged even by accident.

# 1) ignore every file at every depth, but still descend into directories
*
!*/

# 2) re-include known code file types (any depth)
# (There are no *.tmpl / *.plist.tmpl re-includes: no template file exists;
# install-agents.sh renders plists inline via emit_plist.)
!/bin/organism
!*.py
!*.sh
!*.js
!*.json
!*.md
!*.example
!.gitignore
# Without a yml re-include the CI workflow could never ship.
# Targeted (not '!*.yml') to keep the deny-by-default posture for stray yaml.
!/.github/workflows/ci.yml
# README diagrams are hand-drawn SVGs (mermaid needed zoom + pan to read).
# Targeted to docs/img so a stray svg elsewhere stays under the deny-by-default.
!/docs/img/*.svg
# Synthetic transcripts for the renderer tests (JSON Lines).
!/claude/hooks/tests/fixtures/transcripts/*.jsonl

# 3) re-include extensionless code we ship, by tree/glob (no codenames)
!/LICENSE
!/claude/git-hooks/**
# THIS repo's own git hooks (deploy.sh links them into <git-dir>/hooks so `git pull` runs
# converge.sh). Extensionless by git's naming rules, so the `*` deny + extension allowlist
# above would drop them and a fresh clone would silently have no hooks at all.
!/git-hooks/**
!/claude/hooks/health/sudoers-*

# 4) HARD RE-DENY, never commit, even under a re-included tree (overrides §2–3)
.credentials.json
**/state/
**/logs/
**/sessions/
telegram-*.json
telegram-*.txt
*.bak
*.bak-*
*.pyc
__pycache__/
HANDOFF.md
host.json
paths.env
reconcile-pairings.json
# host-local INSTANCE code (e.g. a personal report): per-host, never core, never
# published, run as standalone launchd agents via the gitignored ~/.claude/state/agents.local
# manifest (registered in launchd/install-agents.sh). Reachable via the ~/.claude/hooks
# symlink.
/claude/hooks/local/
# Skills, personal or synced from claude.ai: deploy.sh links ~/.claude/skills here, so every
# skill Claude Code saves lands in this tree. The core ships none; never commit one.
/claude/skills/
# ...but keep the sanitized, codename-free examples (override the re-deny)
!**/paths.env.example
!**/reconcile-pairings.example.json
# case-insensitive macOS FS: the HANDOFF.md re-deny above also matches the
# lowercase /handoff command file, keep that one code file.
!/claude/commands/handoff.md
